 ## Overview
-Latent Diffusion Models (LDM) for 3D perform the diffusion process in a compressed latent space rather than the high-dimensional voxel or pixel space, significantly improving computational efficiency and output quality [S1]. In the context of 3D volume rendering, this approach defines a generative model over latent variables representing scene geometry, enabling the synthesis of voxel-based neural fields [S2]. It sets itself apart from standard Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models (DDPMs) by decoupling the diffusion process from the expensive decoding step, allowing for stable and efficient generation of complex 3D scenes conditioned on hierarchical inputs [S1, S2].
